    "## 6. Economic Performance\n",
    "\n",
    "A stylised trading proxy takes the sign of the forecast price change. Positions are opened every 10 observations and held for 10 observations to avoid overlapping exposure. Ten possible starting offsets assess sensitivity to the trading grid.\n",
    "\n",
    "Transaction costs are **1 basis point per unit of turnover**, including initial entry and final exit. Long-to-short reversals incur two units. Equity starts at one, and initial losses count toward drawdown. Returns and volatility are annualised using **252/10 holding periods per year**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Annualised return, Sharpe and drawdown summaries are suppressed with fewer than 20 non-overlapping holding periods. A multi-month test can still have few independent 10-day trades. The proxy excludes futures rolls, financing, margin and slippage; model selection remains based on forecast MAPE."
   ]
